    <section class="rise-fall" id="timeline" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
      <h2 class="profile-section-title" id="timeline-title">Timeline</h2>
      <ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">c. 1500–1000 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Zarathustra composes the Gathas, by the reckoning of many modern scholars; others place him in the 7th or 6th century BCE</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 520 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-i">Darius I</a> credits his victories to Ahura Mazda in the Behistun inscription</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">224</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardashir-i">Ardashir I</a> founds the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>, under which Zoroastrianism becomes the state religion</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">3rd century</span><span class="rf-text">The high priest Kartir organises the Zoroastrian church and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fire-temple">fire temples</a> across the empire</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">651</span><span class="rf-text">The last Sasanian king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazdegerd-iii">Yazdegerd III</a>, is killed after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muslim-conquest-of-persia">Arab conquest of Iran</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">9th–10th century</span><span class="rf-text">Zoroastrian priests compile the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-persian">Pahlavi</a> books, among them the Denkard and the Bundahishn</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">8th–10th century</span><span class="rf-text">Zoroastrians from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> settle in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, according to the Story of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanjan">Sanjan</a>: the origin of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parsis">Parsis</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1892</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parsis">Parsi</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dadabhai-naoroji">Dadabhai Naoroji</a> becomes the first Asian elected to the British House of Commons</span></li></ol>
    </section>

